      "seconds_since_start": 0.084,
      "seconds_since_previous_block": 0.084
    },
    "text": "This sounds like a Lake Formation cross-account sharing issue \u2014 I can trace through the grant chain (LF permissions, RAM share acceptance, resource links, IAM policies) to find where it's breaking down.\n\nTo look into this, I need a few details:\n\n1. **Producer account ID** (where the database lives) and **consumer account ID** (that can't see it)\n2. **Database name** (and table name, if it's a specific table rather than the whole database)\n3. **Region**\n4. Has the consumer account **accepted the RAM invitation** for the share, and have they tried creating a **resource link** to the shared database in their own Data Catalog?\n\nOnce I have the account IDs and database name, I can start tracing the authorization chain."
